## Conventional Commits (REQUIRED)

All commit messages and PR titles MUST follow conventional commit format:

### Format
```
<type>(<scope>): <description>
```

### Types
- `feat:` - New features
- `fix:` - Bug fixes that affect CLI behavior (not CI, docs, or infrastructure)
- `refactor:` - Code refactoring
- `docs:` - Documentation changes
- `style:` - Code style/formatting (no logic changes)
- `perf:` - Performance improvements
- `test:` - Testing changes
- `chore:` - Maintenance tasks, releases, dependency updates, CI/infrastructure
- `security:` - Security-related changes
- `registry:` - Any changes to `registry/` (no extra scope)

### Examples
```
feat(cli): add new command for tool management
fix(config): resolve parsing issue with nested tables
refactor(backend): simplify plugin loading logic
docs(contributing): update installation instructions
test(e2e): add tests for tool installation
chore(ci): improve cursor cloud agent environment
registry: add miller
```

### Common Scopes
Command names (`install`, `activate`, `use`, `exec`, …) or subsystems:
`config`, `backend`, `env`, `task`, `vfox`, `python`, `github`, `release`,
`completions`, `http`, `schema`, `doctor`, `shim`, `core`, `deps`, `ci`.

Use `task` (not `run`) for task-related changes, even if the code lives in
`src/cli/run.rs` or `src/cmd.rs`.

Description: lowercase after the colon, imperative mood, concise.
